    "background_story": "Savannah was a majestic mare, bred for battle and born for greatness. She was trained by the finest cavalry officers and quickly proved herself to be a warhorse of unyielding courage and strength. During the Great War, Savannah carried her rider, Captain James, into the thick of combat, dodging bullets and artillery fire with ease. Her calm demeanor and instincts kept the Captain safe, even in the most chaotic of battles. Savannah's most notable feat was during the Battle of the Somme, where she led a charge against enemy lines, breaking through the trenches and allowing the Allied forces to gain a crucial foothold. Her bravery and loyalty earned her the respect and admiration of the entire regiment, and she was hailed as a hero upon her return home.",
